From 0d0a9fdc45d8156c3d8fe6ef79dd2989c7e4d741 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 06:46:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Keep native scanner assertions outside modern Bash
 execution skips

Split unchanged security assertions from Bash-version-gated execution proofs so all scanner policy rows run on Bash 3.2. Select the newly landed shared Bash helper as a lane dependency. Routing RED: two missing-helper selection failures; GREEN: focused CI and scanner suites pass. Production scanner policy unchanged.
---
 scripts/ci/classify_changes.py                     |  3 ++-
 tests/ci/test_macos_bash32_routing.py              |  1 +
 tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_comment_words.py   | 13 +++++++++++--
 tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_fd_redirections.py | 13 +++++++++++--
 tests/cron/test_lifecycle_guard_subscript_sink.py  |  7 +++++++
 5 files changed, 32 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/ci/classify_changes.py b/scripts/ci/classify_changes.py
